<title>ITALY: US carrier in Adriatic ahead of Bosnia vote.</title>
<headline>US carrier in Adriatic ahead of Bosnia vote.</headline>
<dateline>NAPLES, Italy 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. aircraft carrier Enterprise returned to the Adriatic on Wednesday to provide air support to peacekeepers in Bosnia if needed during the forthcoming elections, a Sixth Fleet spokesman said.</p>
<p>Bosnia holds its first elections since the end of the four-year civil war on Saturday.</p>
<p>NATO has a 60,000-strong peace force in Bosnia which has promised to provide security for refugees who want to return to their homes to vote.</p>
<p>The U.S. Navy spokesman said the USS Enterprise and its accompanying battle fleet had been on duty in the Mediterranean before heading back into the Adriatic where it regularly patrolled during the war.</p>
</text>
